[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) was merged as one issue and marked known. The reports under it
describe separate problems. Each one has a different fix, so each one gets its own ticket.

## What the reports show

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} {repo} {issues} />

This table counts as the desk counts, like the table on the #4471 page: each report is filed under
its tenant's cause. The reports the desk read as one-day moves stay filed under `parser`, so the
`parser` row counts them as well as the `one-day` row.

<Callout kind="warn">
A fix for one row does not close the others. Keep #4471 for the problem it was written for.
</Callout>

## parser: dates are read month first

The shared parser reads every date month first. A tenant whose locale writes the day first gets
flipped dates: a booking for 7 April arrives as 4 July. This is the problem #4471 was written
for, and its fix is the one already queued.

## hint: the booking-v3 form asks for the wrong order

Booking-v3 prints MM/DD/YYYY under its date field. People at a day-first tenant type what it
says, and the form reads it the tenant's way, so the date flips. A parser fix does not reach
this: the form's hint is wrong, not the parser. Only reports that came through the form, at a
tenant that runs booking-v3, belong here.

## one-day: dates land one day off

These reports describe a date that moved by one day. A flipped month cannot do that. The desk
read them as one-day moves (`desk-notes.json`), and the kb files them under `parser` only
because of the tenant's locale. The cause is not confirmed. One report puts a client in Lisbon
and a client in Toronto on different days for the same meeting, which points at time zones.
Engineering has to reproduce it first.

## How the reports were counted

- Each report is counted once, by id.
- The problem comes from the tenant's locale and booking form, as in `causes.ts`.
- Intake's tag is a guess from the reporter's browser, so it is not used.

## Why one ticket held them all

The desk merges on subject line alone ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)).
The same subjects, such as "Wrong day on the invite", come in for every problem above, so one
rule put all of them into one ticket.

